   "question": "Can CFBD replace PFF grades in the WAR build?",
   "answer": "No - CFBD has no line data and defense is counting stats only.",
   "evidence": "Facets -> adj win pct: PFF 0.826, CFBD 0.741, both 0.845."
  },
  {
   "question": "Should WAR replace PFF as the talent signal?",
   "answer": "No. WAR and PFF are complements, and PFF is the stronger of the two. Swapping PFF out for WAR is the single worst two-source combination.",
   "evidence": "Best blend without PFF 0.2062, without WAR 0.2054, with all three 0.2047. They correlate at only 0.69."
  },
  {
   "question": "Are the blend weights right, or just assembled?",
   "answer": "Right - the shipping 38/38/25 split is the joint optimum of all 45 three-way blends, though the surface is flat.",
   "evidence": "Grid search range 0.2047-0.2088; 7 of 45 blends sit within 0.0005 of the best."
  },
  {
   "question": "Is WAR predictive enough to stand alone?",
   "answer": "No - well behind the O/D composites on its own.",
   "evidence": "As the single feature: WAR 0.2288 vs O/D-only 0.2116."
  },
  {
   "question": "Are talent / returning / WAR the same thing?",
   "answer": "No - returning is nearly orthogonal; talent is the most valuable single feature.",
